## Hero Shell Components (Progressive Loading)

For instant image loading on detail pages, use shell components that only need the media ID:

```tsx
import { HeroBackdropShell, HeroLogoShell } from "@/components/features/media";

// Renders immediately using CDN URLs - no data fetch needed
<HeroBackdropShell
  itemId={movieId}
  mediaType="movie"
  title="Loading..."  // Fallback alt text
  priority
>
  <HeroLogoShell
    itemId={movieId}
    mediaType="movie"
    title="Loading..."  // Fallback text if no logo
    priority
  />
</HeroBackdropShell>
```

**HeroBackdropShell** - Client component for backdrop images:
- Uses CDN URL: `https://image.themoviebrowser.com/{type}/{id}/backdrop.webp`
- Falls back to TMDB `backdrop_path` if CDN fails
- Handles gradient overlays (light/medium/heavy/none)
- Accepts children for content overlay

**HeroLogoShell** - Client component for logo images:
- Uses CDN URL: `https://image.themoviebrowser.com/{type}/{id}/logo.webp`
- Falls back to TMDB logo via `tmdbLogoPath` prop
- Falls back to text title if no logo available
- Three-state loading: cdn → tmdb → text

**Key pattern:** These components work with just `itemId` and `mediaType` (available from URL params), enabling instant image loading before the data fetch completes.

## Hero Section Architecture

The hero sections use a **unified, composable architecture** for visual consistency between homepage carousel and detail pages:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ HeroCarousel (landing page)    │ MediaHero (detail pages)   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│            Aspect-Ratio Container (shared specs)            │
│  aspect-[16/9] md:aspect-[2.2/1] lg:aspect-[2.5/1]         │
│  max-h-[65vh] overflow-hidden                               │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                    MediaBackdrop                            │
│  (handles backdrop image positioning, gradients, overlays)  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          Content Overlay (absolute inset-0 z-10)           │
│          flex flex-col justify-end                          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                     HeroContent                             │
│  (logo, genres, ratings, watch options - bottom aligned)    │
│  pb-5 md:pb-6 lg:pb-8 max-w-xl lg:max-w-2xl                │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
│                                                             │
│  MediaActionBar (separate component, below hero)            │
│  Play Trailer, Watchlist, Like/Dislike, Share              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Unified Container Structure

**CRITICAL**: Both `HeroCarousel` and `MediaHero` MUST use identical container specs for seamless transitions.

The hero uses CSS variables (defined in `globals.css`) for easily tweakable responsive sizing:

```css
/* globals.css - Hero Section Layout Variables */
:root {
  /* Hero height constraints */
  --hero-height-target: 60vh;
  --hero-height-min: 400px;
  --hero-height-max: 800px;
  --hero-height-mobile-target: 50vh;
  --hero-height-mobile-min: 300px;
  --hero-height-mobile-max: 500px;

  /* Hero content width (desktop): target 30vw, min 280px, max 480px */
  --hero-content-width-target: 30vw;
  --hero-content-min-width: 280px;
  --hero-content-max-width: 480px;

  /* Mobile content width: target 85vw, min 260px, max 400px */
  --hero-content-mobile-width-target: 85vw;
  --hero-content-mobile-min-width: 260px;
  --hero-content-mobile-max-width: 400px;
}

/* Hero container uses height-based sizing with max-height cap */
.hero-container {
  width: 100%;
  height: clamp(
    var(--hero-height-mobile-min),
    var(--hero-height-mobile-target),
    var(--hero-height-mobile-max)
  );
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .hero-container {
    height: clamp(
      var(--hero-height-min),
      var(--hero-height-target),
      var(--hero-height-max)
    );
    max-height: 60vh;  /* Cap at 60% of viewport */
  }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**
- Height-based sizing ensures hero never takes more than 60% of viewport
- `clamp()` provides smooth responsive behavior between min/max bounds
- Image positioning (`objectPosition: "85% 20%"`) shows top-right of image to preserve important content

```tsx
// Container uses .hero-container class for CSS variable-based height
<div className="hero-container relative w-full overflow-hidden">
  <MediaBackdrop ... className="absolute inset-0" />

  {/* Content overlay - positioned at bottom */}
  <div className="absolute inset-0 z-10 flex flex-col justify-end px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12">
    {/* HeroContent uses .hero-content-width class for CSS variable-based width */}
    <HeroContent ... className="pb-5 md:pb-6 lg:pb-8" />
  </div>
</div>
```

### Shared Components

**`MediaBackdrop`** / **`HeroBackdropShell`** - Prime Video-style backdrop:

**Desktop (md+):**
- Image positioned to the right: `left-0 md:left-[18%] lg:left-[25%]`
- `object-cover` with `objectPosition: "85% 20%"` - 85% from left (right bias), 20% from top (shows more top of image)
- Black background base for clean left gradient fade
- Gradient fade from black on image's left edge (35-50% width)
- Subtle bottom gradient (10-28% height depending on overlay intensity)
- Three overlay presets: `light`, `medium`, `heavy`
- MUST have `h-full` on children wrapper for flexbox to work

**Mobile (<md):**
- Full-bleed `object-cover` fills entire container
- `object-[center_20%]` - centered horizontally, 20% from top (shows faces/important content)
- Enhanced bottom gradient for content readability (95% opacity at bottom → transparent at 60%)
- No left gradient needed (content overlays the image)

**`HeroContent`** - Content layout (bottom-aligned):
- Uses `.hero-content-width` class for responsive width (30vw desktop, 85vw mobile with min/max)
- Logo (with responsive constraints: `max-w-[220px] md:max-w-[420px] lg:max-w-[520px]`)
- Gap between logo and info: `mb-4 md:mb-6 lg:mb-8`
- Genres → Ratings → Watch Options (compact vertical stack)
- Shared animation variants (`heroContainerVariants`, `heroItemVariants`)
- **No actions prop** - actions moved to separate `MediaActionBar`
- **Text shadows for mobile**: `[text-shadow:0_1px_3px_rgba(0,0,0,0.8)]` on content containers for readability over backdrop
- **Drop shadow on logo**: `drop-shadow-lg` applied to logo container

**`MediaActionBar`** - Action buttons (separate from hero):
- Play Trailer, Watchlist toggle, Like/Dislike, Share
- Positioned between hero and overview with negative margin
- `className="px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12 -mt-8 md:-mt-10 lg:-mt-12 relative z-20"`

```tsx
import { MediaHero, MediaActionBar } from "@/components/features/media";

// Detail page usage:
<MediaHero item={movie} mediaType="movie" />
<MediaActionBar
  itemId={movie.id}
  mediaType="movie"
  title={movie.title}
  trailer={trailer}
  className="px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12 -mt-8 md:-mt-10 relative z-20"
/>
<MediaOverview item={movie} mediaType="movie" />

// HeroCarousel (landing page) - uses heroEnhancedData from getTrending()
<HeroCarousel
  items={trending.allItems}
  heroEnhancedData={trending.heroEnhancedData}  // Ratings + watch options per item
/>
```

### Design Specs

- **Container**: `aspect-[16/9] md:aspect-[2.2/1] lg:aspect-[2.5/1] max-h-[65vh]`
- **Content positioning**: `flex flex-col justify-end` with bottom padding
- **Content max-width**: `max-w-xl lg:max-w-2xl` (prevents text spanning full width)
- **HeroCarousel**: Fully clickable (navigates to detail page)
- **Action buttons**: Glassmorphism style (`bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 backdrop-blur-sm`)

## RatingsBar Component

Unified ratings display showing scores from multiple sources. Only 5 sources are displayed (whitelisted):

| Source | Scale | Display Format | Example |
|--------|-------|----------------|---------|
| TMDB | 0-10 | Decimal | 7.6 |
| IMDb | 0-10 | Decimal | 7.3 |
| RT Critic | 0-100 | Integer % | 86 |
| RT Audience | 0-100 | Integer % | 95 |
| Google | 0-100 | Integer % | 93 |

Metacritic and Letterboxd are captured in the database but filtered out in the UI.

```tsx
import { RatingsBar } from "@/components/features/media";

// Basic usage with ratings from movie/series
<RatingsBar ratings={movie.ratings} size="md" />

// Fallback to TMDB-only when no external ratings
<RatingsBar
  ratings={movie.ratings?.length
    ? movie.ratings
    : [{ name: "TMDB", rating: Math.round(movie.vote_average * 10).toString() }]
  }
/>

// Rating format: { name: string, rating: string, link?: string, certified?: boolean }
// - TMDB/IMDb: rating = "7.6" (0-10 scale, displayed as-is with decimal)
// - RT/Google: rating = "86%" (0-100 scale, displayed as integer)
```

**Design principles:**
- Single grouped pill container (not separate pills per source)
- Ratings separated by subtle `border-white/15` dividers
- Icon + color-coded score for each source
- Muted color palette: `hsl(h, 50%, 55%)` for scores
- Sizes: `sm` (cards), `md` (hero), `lg` (detail sections)

**Vertical alignment pattern:**
```tsx
// Use fixed-height wrapper for icons to ensure alignment
<div className={cn("relative flex-shrink-0", heightClass)} style={{ width: iconSize }}>
  <Image src={icon} fill className="object-contain" unoptimized />
</div>
```

