### Video Gallery with YouTube Integration

The VideoGallery component displays YouTube videos with rich metadata from the YouTube Data API.

**Component Structure:**
```
src/components/features/media/
├── video-gallery.tsx      # Main gallery component
├── video-stats.tsx        # Stats display (views, likes, comments, channel)
└── video-comments.tsx     # Comments section with expand/collapse
```

**Features:**
- Batch fetches metadata for all videos on mount (up to 50 per API call)
- Fetches full data (stats + 100 comments) for active video
- Shows view count, comment count, like/dislike bar, channel info
- Comments in a card with show more/less toggle
- Sidebar at 25% width with video thumbnails

**Stats Row Layout:**
```tsx
// Views • Comments • Like/Dislike bar (all inline)
<div className="flex items-center gap-4">
  <div className="flex items-center gap-3 text-muted-foreground">
    <div className="flex items-center gap-1">
      <Eye className="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      <span className="text-xs font-medium">{formatViewCount(viewCount)}</span>
    </div>
    <div className="flex items-center gap-1">
      <MessageCircle className="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      <span className="text-xs font-medium">{formatViewCount(commentCount)}</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <InlineLikeBar likes={likeCount} dislikes={dislikeCount} />
</div>
```

### Video Gallery Height Sync

Sync sidebar scroll area height with main player:

```tsx
const mainPlayerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
const [playerHeight, setPlayerHeight] = useState(0);

useEffect(() => {
  const updateHeight = () => {
    if (mainPlayerRef.current) {
      setPlayerHeight(mainPlayerRef.current.offsetHeight);
    }
  };
  updateHeight();
  window.addEventListener("resize", updateHeight);
  return () => window.removeEventListener("resize", updateHeight);
}, []);

// Sidebar at 25% width
<div className="w-[25%] min-w-[280px] max-w-[400px] flex-shrink-0">
  <ScrollArea style={{ height: `${playerHeight + 60}px` }}>
```

### Inline Video Playback

Videos should play in-place, not in modals:

```tsx
const [isPlaying, setIsPlaying] = useState(false);

{isPlaying ? (
  <iframe
    src={`https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/${videoKey}?autoplay=1&rel=0`}
    allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media"
    allowFullScreen
    className="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full"
  />
) : (
  <>
    <Image src={thumbnailUrl} fill />
    <button onClick={() => setIsPlaying(true)}>
      <Play />
    </button>
  </>
)}
```

